{"id": "EUVD-2026-72805", "enisaUuid": "1c105636-77e6-351d-9d68-2f4c65d81664", "description": "Netis NX10 firmware V4.0.1.5808 and V3.0.0.4142 contain an information disclosure vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to retrieve the administrator password by sending a request to the sysinfo action in the web management interface without a valid session. Attackers can replay the exposed credential against the login handler to establish a fully authenticated administrator session on the device.", "datePublished": "2026-09-08T14:23:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-19T14:21:56", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackwithmike.com/research/netis/2026-09", "https://hackwithmike.com/research/advisories/netis/cve-2026-61516", "https://www.netis-systems.com/products/NX10.html", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netis-nx10-credential-disclosure-via-sysinfo-diagnostic-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-61516", "GHSA-p7mp-88jw-8275"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.71, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a0b2307-ad88-3c44-9341-feeb448fd9c3", "product": {"name": "NX10", "vendor": {"name": "Netis Systems"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0.4142"}, {"id": "64bed7f9-cb43-3a93-83a7-036e69ab6985", "product": {"name": "NX10", "vendor": {"name": "Netis Systems"}}, "product_version": "4.0.1.5808"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9418892b-447c-3d68-9074-8bed98afa48d", "vendor": {"name": "Netis Systems"}}], "isExploited": false}